From: Ladislav Laska <krakonos@krakonos.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: qcom-ipq9574: report USXGMII link from XPCS block lock

The AQR113C on the Compex AP.AL02.3 completes USXGMII auto-negotiation
with the XPCS (speed is passed correctly in VR_MII_AN_INTR_STS) but never
sets the link bit of the control word, so with in-band mode phylink never
saw the PCS link come up. The vendor QSDK takes the link from the PHY and
reads the same 0 there.

In-band AN is required on this link: with USX auto-negotiation disabled on
the PHY (which phylink does in PHY mode) the data path stays dead in both
directions even though the XPCS has block lock.

For single-channel USXGMII (not 10G-QXGMII), fall back to the XPCS
64b/66b block lock when the AN link bit is clear. phylink ANDs the PCS
link with the PHY link in in-band mode.

Signed-off-by: Ladislav Laska <krakonos@krakonos.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -253,6 +253,19 @@ static void ipq_pcs_get_state_usxgmii(st
 
 	state->link = !!(val & XPCS_USXG_AN_LINK_STS);
 
+	/* The AQR113C completes USXGMII auto-negotiation and passes the
+	 * negotiated speed, but never sets the link bit in its control word,
+	 * also not under the vendor QSDK. On a single-channel USXGMII link,
+	 * fall back to the 64b/66b block lock of the XPCS; phylink ANDs this
+	 * with the PHY link state anyway.
+	 */
+	if (!state->link && state->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII) {
+		unsigned int kr;
+
+		ret = regmap_read(qpcs->regmap, XPCS_KR_STS, &kr);
+		state->link = !ret && (kr & XPCS_KR_LINK_STS);
+	}
+
 	if (!state->link)
 		return;
 
